WEBVTT

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:25.250
This is for our boss! Don't let him run, after him!

00:00:49.270 --> 00:00:52.070
Get up and look for him! Don't let him get away!

00:00:54.700 --> 00:00:56.990
Christ, what the hell is he?

00:00:56.990 --> 00:01:01.790
We had our boss under extra-heavy guard, and he took him out with just one shot?

00:01:06.500 --> 00:01:07.710
Y-You bastard!

00:01:07.710 --> 00:01:10.710
You even got yourself a damn getaway plane?!

00:01:41.740 --> 00:01:46.910
I walk unsteadily on paths to nowhere

00:01:47.120 --> 00:01:51.040
wondering what I should do right now.

00:01:52.550 --> 00:01:57.510
I play the song you like on the car stereo

00:01:57.680 --> 00:02:02.060
with the volume up and my feelings crystallized

00:02:02.060 --> 00:02:07.690
driving on streets with no crossroads or signals

00:02:07.890 --> 00:02:13.110
with a speed that will catch up with you.

00:02:13.440 --> 00:02:17.570
So faraway - let's run!

00:02:17.900 --> 00:02:23.870
And let's not bother with the breaks - full throttle.

00:02:24.160 --> 00:02:28.160
Oh someday - one of these days

00:02:28.370 --> 00:02:33.250
You'll be at my place where nobody can find you.

00:02:33.840 --> 00:02:39.340
Whenever you suffer a breakdown one can't see

00:02:39.590 --> 00:02:44.930
depend on me for your repairs.

00:02:45.180 --> 00:02:49.310
So faraway - let's run!

00:02:49.520 --> 00:02:55.530
We'll reset and start again - even at our limit.

00:02:55.730 --> 00:02:59.820
Oh someday - one of these days

00:03:00.030 --> 00:03:05.870
If I'm with you we'll find our dream.

00:03:51.500 --> 00:03:56.250
Armored Trooper SDR2

00:04:35.210 --> 00:04:36.290
Who are you?

00:04:36.290 --> 00:04:39.800
I... I am an Arab militant.

00:04:40.210 --> 00:04:41.710
And the others?

00:04:41.710 --> 00:04:46.550
I don't know their circumstances, but they're probably captured terrorists.

00:04:47.010 --> 00:04:48.100
Terrorists?

00:04:49.510 --> 00:04:50.560
How many?

00:04:50.560 --> 00:04:54.640
There were about fifty of us... but most of us are dead!

00:04:54.640 --> 00:04:58.980
Everyone was brought to this island and was forced into a death match!

00:04:58.980 --> 00:04:59.940
Death match?

00:04:59.940 --> 00:05:01.070
Y-Yes.

00:05:01.480 --> 00:05:06.320
They said it was a death match to see who will be the last to survive and leave the island.

00:05:06.780 --> 00:05:07.410
What?

00:05:08.320 --> 00:05:09.990
We were tricked!

00:05:09.990 --> 00:05:13.700
They actually brought us to this island to massacre all of us-

00:05:55.790 --> 00:05:57.580
What was that just now?

00:05:58.620 --> 00:06:01.590
I don't know. There's no data available.

00:06:04.590 --> 00:06:08.590
It might be a crew member from
that light aircraft that just crashed.

00:06:09.220 --> 00:06:10.390
What?

00:06:10.390 --> 00:06:15.180
The drug cartels around here do employ aerial smugglers.

00:06:15.600 --> 00:06:18.600
Whoever he is, we can't let him leave here alive.

00:06:19.730 --> 00:06:21.650
We'll kill him with the rest.

00:06:28.740 --> 00:06:30.160
<i>A minefield?</i>

00:06:37.410 --> 00:06:39.120
Right foot, one meter away

00:06:39.120 --> 00:06:42.590
One Chinese Type 72A land mine spotted.

00:06:43.340 --> 00:06:45.210
Disregard! Maintain forward progress!

00:06:57.770 --> 00:07:03.060
The body of the SDR2 is armored just like an Abrams tank.

00:07:03.060 --> 00:07:05.780
Anti-personnel land mines will not affect it in the least.

00:07:12.280 --> 00:07:17.660
I've spotted a TM62M anti-tank mine at a point two meters from the left foot.

00:07:18.040 --> 00:07:21.790
Adjust your route five degrees to your right and detour.

00:07:21.790 --> 00:07:22.540
Ten-four.

00:07:38.470 --> 00:07:40.810
It would have been ugly if that were a direct hit.

00:07:41.270 --> 00:07:43.810
Why did the mine explode?

00:07:43.810 --> 00:07:46.320
It was hit with a rifle bullet.

00:07:46.320 --> 00:07:48.320
It's just a coincidence, shrug it off.

00:07:53.740 --> 00:07:57.120
The target is right in front of me hiding in the western thickets.

00:07:57.120 --> 00:07:58.950
Incinerate with the flame thrower.

00:07:58.950 --> 00:07:59.830
Affirmative!

00:08:28.190 --> 00:08:29.690
I've lost sight of the target!

00:08:30.610 --> 00:08:32.030
What happened to the target!

00:08:32.030 --> 00:08:33.360
Settle down!

00:08:33.360 --> 00:08:35.240
Stand by for our orders!

00:08:35.910 --> 00:08:36.660
Acknowledged.

00:08:39.660 --> 00:08:43.330
Did he fall into the sea or get splattered on the rocks?

00:08:43.330 --> 00:08:46.420
Whatever's the case, his chances of surviving are slim.

00:08:46.420 --> 00:08:48.250
Do a search with the geophone.

00:08:48.250 --> 00:08:49.170
Ten-four.

00:08:49.170 --> 00:08:50.550
Geophone?

00:08:50.550 --> 00:08:55.760
It's an instrument which picks up sound waves traveling along the ground and amplifies them by the thousands.

00:08:55.760 --> 00:08:58.550
If there's anything moving, we'll know immediately.

00:08:59.180 --> 00:09:03.270
The pilot's blood pressure and heart rate are increasing!

00:09:03.270 --> 00:09:07.770
Don't worry, that's a normal condition for a soldier in a battlefield.

00:09:07.770 --> 00:09:10.900
Hasn't it been only three months since he enlisted?

00:09:10.900 --> 00:09:15.200
I really doubt if he could withstand this heavy carnage psychologically!

00:09:15.200 --> 00:09:19.240
The entire operation is being
composed by this supercomputer.

00:09:19.240 --> 00:09:22.200
All the pilot has to do is follow the orders.

00:09:22.200 --> 00:09:27.210
He's not going to suffer from mental problems like the soldiers who returned from Vietnam.

00:09:27.210 --> 00:09:29.500
You're willing to assert that?

00:09:29.500 --> 00:09:31.170
We've detected some footsteps.

00:09:31.170 --> 00:09:32.210
What?

00:09:32.210 --> 00:09:35.220
It's not from the jungle, but from inside the town.

00:09:35.220 --> 00:09:37.300
So it's not from that guy we saw earlier.

00:09:37.300 --> 00:09:40.510
We've already confirmed 49 dead.

00:09:40.510 --> 00:09:42.850
The only one left is Noyce.

00:09:43.270 --> 00:09:44.930
Hmm? Noyce?

00:09:54.860 --> 00:09:59.450
Noyce is a former IRA member. He's the last one left.

00:09:59.450 --> 00:10:00.370
Affirmative.

00:10:11.920 --> 00:10:14.710
So you wanna play, huh Noyce?

00:10:14.710 --> 00:10:16.760
He planted that bomb?

00:10:16.760 --> 00:10:20.180
That's right. Noyce is a bomb specialist.

00:10:20.180 --> 00:10:24.470
Roads, churches... if you build it he'll blow it up.

00:10:24.470 --> 00:10:27.390
He's been this test's most difficult opponent.

00:10:30.770 --> 00:10:32.150
Eat shit!

00:10:47.540 --> 00:10:48.830
All normal.

00:10:48.830 --> 00:10:50.880
The SDR2 is still functioning.

00:10:50.880 --> 00:10:52.540
There's hardly even a scratch!

00:10:52.540 --> 00:10:58.550
Excellent! Our soldiers are sure to jump for joy once we deploy these to the front lines.

00:10:59.340 --> 00:11:00.130
Chief.

00:11:00.130 --> 00:11:01.050
Hmm? What now?

00:11:01.050 --> 00:11:04.470
The pilot's brainwaves have become a bit irregular.

00:11:04.470 --> 00:11:05.680
What?

00:11:05.680 --> 00:11:08.560
We can still live with it, but if it gets any worse...

00:11:08.560 --> 00:11:09.440
Shh!

00:11:09.440 --> 00:11:11.440
Do you want to put a stop to the test?

00:11:11.440 --> 00:11:15.860
Over $100 million is riding on this SDR2 project!

00:11:35.170 --> 00:11:37.250
SDR2, what's wrong?

00:11:37.250 --> 00:11:38.920
Why aren't you using your Gatling gun?

00:11:39.380 --> 00:11:42.340
I'd just be wasting my bullets on this guy!

00:11:42.930 --> 00:11:44.300
What?

00:11:45.430 --> 00:11:49.430
Looks like the battlefield has taken over our soldier.

00:11:49.810 --> 00:11:50.680
Y... Yeah.

00:11:58.690 --> 00:12:00.530
D-Desist!

00:12:00.530 --> 00:12:03.200
Don't do more than necessary, SDR2!

00:12:03.660 --> 00:12:07.240
I have to! There's a slight possibility he might revive!

00:12:07.700 --> 00:12:11.750
Revive? What the hell's the meaning of this?

00:12:11.750 --> 00:12:13.210
W-Well...

00:12:13.210 --> 00:12:16.590
I knew it, his mental state is deteriorating.

00:12:16.590 --> 00:12:18.250
W-What's your basis?

00:12:17.880 --> 00:12:23.300
Flesh-and-blood humans aren't meant to deal
with all this carnage with their minds fully intact.

00:12:23.300 --> 00:12:29.140
If you officially deploy that thing, your American soldiers will develop even bigger mental scars!

00:12:29.140 --> 00:12:30.930
What are you saying?

00:12:30.930 --> 00:12:36.480
We did not sponsor your robotics development in order to make this killing machine!

00:12:36.480 --> 00:12:38.110
This is a weapon from hell!

00:12:38.110 --> 00:12:41.150
That soldier's mind will never return back to normal!

00:12:43.820 --> 00:12:44.910
And what of it?

00:12:46.410 --> 00:12:49.620
There's no such thing as "sanity" on the battlefield.

00:12:49.620 --> 00:12:53.710
Back in Vietnam, we ate bullets fired by women and children.

00:12:53.710 --> 00:12:56.670
A bunch of my soldiers got killed because we let our guards down.

00:12:56.670 --> 00:13:01.420
That's why it makes perfect sense
to put that in play during wartime.

00:13:01.420 --> 00:13:03.220
B-But...

00:13:03.220 --> 00:13:05.220
Mm-hmm. I say it's a success.

00:13:05.220 --> 00:13:11.770
We'll just toss our soldiers into those SDR2s and reprogram their minds in battle.

00:13:11.770 --> 00:13:13.430
Th-Thank you.

00:13:13.930 --> 00:13:15.810
You're mad.

00:13:15.810 --> 00:13:17.940
Every one of you is touched in the head!

00:13:18.360 --> 00:13:20.230
I'm through with this!

00:13:22.030 --> 00:13:24.530
Hmph. Peace-loving nip.

00:13:24.860 --> 00:13:28.320
Now then, let's retrieve the SDR2 and call it a day.

00:13:27.950 --> 00:13:31.040
Wait. There's still one left.

00:13:31.040 --> 00:13:31.950
What?

00:13:34.250 --> 00:13:35.960
It's the guy from before!

00:14:02.150 --> 00:14:05.650
Color me surprised. So you're still alive, huh?

00:14:05.650 --> 00:14:07.530
Shoot him with the rifle now!

00:14:07.530 --> 00:14:09.570
Distance: 600 meters.

00:14:09.570 --> 00:14:10.910
Wind speed: 5 meters per second.

00:14:10.910 --> 00:14:12.740
Humidity: 80 percent.

00:14:13.240 --> 00:14:14.540
Adjustments complete.

00:14:19.500 --> 00:14:21.960
Damn. He missed?

00:14:21.960 --> 00:14:25.630
There seemed to be an updraft from the intervening valley.

00:14:25.630 --> 00:14:27.510
This time don't miss!

00:14:32.010 --> 00:14:34.680
He was shot in the face shield!

00:14:34.680 --> 00:14:35.720
What?

00:14:35.720 --> 00:14:39.520
He was able to hit us from the
distance that the SDR2 missed?

00:14:39.520 --> 00:14:43.520
I... If it weren't for the bullet-proof glass, I'd be killed!

00:14:53.450 --> 00:14:55.370
Stop that, SDR2!

00:14:55.370 --> 00:14:57.450
Don't shoot until the adjustments are made!

00:14:57.450 --> 00:15:00.830
What just happened was only a fluke! Don't go nuts!

00:15:01.920 --> 00:15:03.000
<i>No...</i>

00:15:03.000 --> 00:15:05.300
<i>That wasn't a fluke.</i>

00:15:05.300 --> 00:15:07.460
<i>That was something he aimed for and hit on target.</i>

00:15:17.850 --> 00:15:22.060
H-He's disappeared somewhere. I can't get his location anywhere.

00:15:22.060 --> 00:15:22.600
What?

00:15:22.600 --> 00:15:23.860
What do you mean?

00:15:23.860 --> 00:15:27.860
Well, we were able to track him all the way to the south stream, but...

00:15:53.340 --> 00:15:55.350
I-I spotted the target!

00:15:55.350 --> 00:15:56.760
He was right there.

00:15:58.560 --> 00:16:00.770
He rubbed mud all over his body.

00:16:00.770 --> 00:16:06.650
I see, he covered himself with mud in order to evade the infrared vision.

00:16:06.650 --> 00:16:09.230
Doing that will lower the body temperature.

00:16:21.910 --> 00:16:25.080
You bastard, now you want to lure us into the river?

00:16:25.080 --> 00:16:27.040
Use the Owl Eye!

00:16:27.040 --> 00:16:29.880
Owl Eye? You mean the night-vision scope?

00:16:29.880 --> 00:16:35.930
Yes. It amplifies faint rays of light by tens
of thousands. There's no way he can hide.

00:16:46.730 --> 00:16:48.440
The Owl Eye's caught sight of him.

00:16:52.610 --> 00:16:54.610
Target... locked!

00:17:11.050 --> 00:17:12.630
M-My eyes!

00:17:14.010 --> 00:17:16.720
That flare has overblown the monitor!

00:17:16.720 --> 00:17:18.300
S-Say that again?

00:17:19.100 --> 00:17:23.890
The night-vision scope automatically closes its shutters if it encounters bright lights.

00:17:23.890 --> 00:17:27.310
He fired his flare because he knew that.

00:17:28.400 --> 00:17:31.820
This is not an easy enemy we are dealing with.

00:17:33.070 --> 00:17:34.950
Calm down, SDR2!

00:17:35.570 --> 00:17:37.200
Your eyesight will soon return!

00:17:42.490 --> 00:17:44.910
SDR2, settle down!

00:17:44.910 --> 00:17:46.580
Your target is at nine o'clock!

00:18:13.280 --> 00:18:14.940
It's... It's them!

00:18:14.940 --> 00:18:16.400
They're... still alive!

00:18:21.330 --> 00:18:24.700
Die!

00:18:27.660 --> 00:18:29.790
Desist, SDR2!

00:18:29.790 --> 00:18:31.290
Those are corpses!

00:18:32.420 --> 00:18:35.670
Chief, the pilot is now completely deranged!

00:18:35.670 --> 00:18:37.800
Stop the test immediately!

00:18:37.800 --> 00:18:39.180
If you don't, he'll...

00:18:40.090 --> 00:18:41.760
Continue.

00:18:41.760 --> 00:18:44.930
Whatever happens, we need to see how this ends.

00:19:20.880 --> 00:19:21.930
The...

00:19:21.930 --> 00:19:24.640
The SDR2... is completely destroyed!

00:19:36.400 --> 00:19:42.110
That guy took perfect aim and shot a bullet straight through the muzzle!

00:19:42.110 --> 00:19:43.910
No, that's impossible!

00:19:43.910 --> 00:19:48.830
That's the man who can hit the SDR2's face from that long of a distance.

00:19:48.830 --> 00:19:50.910
I'm not surprised he pulled this off.

00:19:51.580 --> 00:19:54.920
That sort of man really exists?

00:19:55.500 --> 00:19:57.210
Get that man here, now!

00:19:57.210 --> 00:19:57.920
Sir!

00:19:58.840 --> 00:20:01.880
I will find out exactly who he is.

00:20:05.970 --> 00:20:13.190
...so we've gathered a group of terrorists in
order to test out the SDR2's combat abilities.

00:20:14.100 --> 00:20:17.440
The SDR2 was supposed to be the last to survive, but...

00:20:17.440 --> 00:20:22.200
...I hate to say it, but you, the last-
minute competitor, lasted to the end.

00:20:23.450 --> 00:20:30.450
So because of that, we want you to tell us
how you attained your combat abilities.

00:20:32.500 --> 00:20:34.460
What will you do once you know?

00:20:34.460 --> 00:20:41.380
America will be involved in conflicts in the remote
reaches the world in order to protect her freedoms.

00:20:41.380 --> 00:20:47.720
However, today's youth do not have the force of will necessary to take part in any land wars.

00:20:48.180 --> 00:20:51.480
Meaning you can't have an army that only relies on aerial bombings?

00:20:51.480 --> 00:20:53.310
That's right.

00:20:53.310 --> 00:21:00.530
If we make use of your combat know-how, we can rapidly improve our military training and create a truly potent army.

00:21:00.530 --> 00:21:05.490
Plus we won't need to blow an
asston of money on some SDR2!

00:21:05.490 --> 00:21:06.990
N-Now wait...

00:21:08.530 --> 00:21:12.500
Please become an adviser to our armed forces.

00:21:12.500 --> 00:21:14.410
And if I refuse?

00:21:16.330 --> 00:21:18.340
Sorry, but you can't do that.

00:21:18.340 --> 00:21:21.000
This is not a request - it's an order!

00:21:25.800 --> 00:21:29.760
You can only give "yes" for an answer.

00:21:42.860 --> 00:21:45.700
Why did you collect only terrorists?

00:21:46.400 --> 00:21:54.410
Those unforgivable bastards are destroying all that is just which our soldiers have built up all over the globe!

00:21:55.870 --> 00:22:00.420
And what is "just" is what you all decide is just, isn't it?

00:22:00.420 --> 00:22:04.420
Quit bullshitting! What's right for America is right for the world!

00:22:43.880 --> 00:22:47.170
I  was worried with no one to talk to.

00:22:47.170 --> 00:22:50.220
I was brooding and standing still

00:22:50.220 --> 00:22:52.390
without moving a muscle.

00:22:53.050 --> 00:22:55.560
I wonder when that was?

00:22:56.060 --> 00:22:57.270
I'm sure

00:22:57.270 --> 00:23:00.440
you agonized over how

00:23:00.440 --> 00:23:05.690
people will hurt themselves and other people

00:23:06.320 --> 00:23:08.950
and fail to realize it.

00:23:09.320 --> 00:23:10.070
When

00:23:10.070 --> 00:23:13.490
the same days keep repeating themselves

00:23:13.490 --> 00:23:15.740
you never change.

00:23:16.450 --> 00:23:18.000
Since you're here for me

00:23:18.000 --> 00:23:22.290
I will accept the way that I am.

00:23:23.000 --> 00:23:26.550
I will never leave you alone

00:23:26.550 --> 00:23:29.880
I will softly touch your trembling heart.

00:23:30.090 --> 00:23:36.770
I realized that I'm not the only one who's alone.

00:23:36.770 --> 00:23:39.940
We're enveloped in the gentle sun beams.

00:23:39.940 --> 00:23:43.270
The long winter is finally over.

00:23:43.270 --> 00:23:49.900
The parts of us that were lonely will surely get stronger.

00:24:01.250 --> 00:24:05.090
Golgo's right arm ceased to move after an accident.

00:24:05.090 --> 00:24:10.510
In order to carry out a job, he entrusts the surgical operation to the "angel arms" of Dr. Yang.

00:24:11.170 --> 00:24:15.760
But he also knows that the target is Yang's adoptive parent.

00:24:15.760 --> 00:24:19.140
So what choice will the sniper with the arms of the devil make?

00:24:19.390 --> 00:24:25.520
Arms of an Angel, Arms of The Devil

00:24:20.180 --> 00:24:24.480
Next time on Golgo 13: Arms of an Angel, Arms of The Devil.

00:24:24.480 --> 00:24:28.480
Don't stand behind him, if you value your life.
